\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Radio safety at the admission boundary on two nodes. (a) End of the last recovery in every attempt of the bound-padded boundary diagnostic. E4 offers a 256-token request with two required recoveries at 45\nonbreakingspace ms; E6b and E6a offer a 64-token request with one required recovery at 89 and 88\nonbreakingspace ms. Baseline attempts launch the request anyway: idle-time admission in E4 and a forced launch of the request that Backstop\xspace  rejects in E6b. (b) AI requests per prompt length in the two-node campaign: requests that Backstop\xspace  runs and requests that it rejects because the required recoveries would then miss the recovery deadline; idle-time admission would run all of them, and static reservation runs none.}}{20}{figure.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
